<article class="env-lemma" id="08EI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/08EI">Lemma <span data-tag="08EI">36.13.8</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an affine scheme. Let $U \subset X$ be a quasi-compact open. For every perfect object $F$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ the object $F \oplus F[1]$ is the restriction of a perfect object of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/08EG" data-tag="08EG">36.13.6</a> we can find a perfect object $E$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ such that $E|_ U = \mathcal{F}[r] \oplus F$ for some finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ U$-module $\mathcal{F}$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/08EH" data-tag="08EH">36.13.7</a> we can find a morphism of perfect complexes $\alpha : E_1 \to E$ such that $(E_1)|_ U \cong E|_ U$ and such that $\alpha |_ U$ is the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \left( \begin{matrix}  \text{id}_{\mathcal{F}[r]} 

&  0 

\\  0 

&  0 

\end{matrix} \right) : \mathcal{F}[r] \oplus F \to \mathcal{F}[r] \oplus F  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Then the cone on $\alpha $ is a solution. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>